<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    The register an indirect call jumps through, when it is also an argument
    slot in front of a live one.

        s5:  inc %rsi; jmp *%rdi

    is `void s5(void (*fp)(void *, long), long x) { fp((void *)fp, x + 1); }`
    (clang -O2): the target is passed to itself.  `passthrough` reads the
    register a call jumps through as no argument of its own
    (kuna_passthrough.rs, is_call_target), because `onlyOpUse` takes the
    call's read of the trial slot as the parameter use and never looks at
    slot 0.  Scored definitely-not-used, that trial made forceNoUse drop every
    argument after it too, so the call printed `(*a0)()` and lost `x + 1`.  It
    is scored inactive instead: dropped from the end of a list, as the target
    r8 of kuna-callproto.xml is, and filled below a later argument, where the
    ABI's order makes it the first one.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring", option `passthrough`
    (is_call_target applies in both passes).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
48ffc6ffe7
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="s5"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option passthrough off</com>
  <com>lo fu s5</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option passthrough on</com>
  <com>lo fu s5</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="passthrough-calltarget #1: the target passed to itself stays an argument in front of the live one" min="2" max="2">\(\*a0\)\(a0,a1 \+ 1\); // jump-as-call</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
